      "math_academy_id": "q-115667",
      "knowledge_point_id": "a78860ea-192f-5df9-aca9-4f67ec6ffefe",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating a Rational Function Given Part Of the Partial Fraction Decomposition",
      "problem": "Given that \n\n$$\n\\frac{4{x}^{2}+20}{(x+2)({x}^{2}+8)}=\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}+8}+\\frac{D}{x+2},\n$$\n\nwhere $D$ is a constant to be found, calculate $\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+20}{(x+2)({x}^{2}+8)}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we find the constant $D.$ Multiplying both sides of the given equality by $(x+2)({x}^{2}+8)$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+20 & =(x-2)(x+2)+D({x}^{2}+8).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x=0$  into the above gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4(0)^{2}+20 & =(0-2)(0+2)+D({0}^{2}+8) \\\\ 20 & =-4+8D \\\\ 24 & =8D \\\\ D & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+20}{(x+2)({x}^{2}+8)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{x-2}{{x}^{2}+8}+\\frac{3}{x+2})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}x-2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use the substitution ${x}^{2}+8=u.$ Then, $x\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x}{{x}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\frac{1}{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+8).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+8}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+(2\\sqrt{2})^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{2}}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{2\\sqrt{2}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\cdot \\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}x}{4}).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we get\n\n$$\n3\\int \\frac{1}{x+2}\\text{d}x=3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4{x}^{2}+20}{(x+2)({x}^{2}+8)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+8)-\\frac{\\sqrt{2}}{2}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{\\sqrt{2}x}{4})+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x+2|+C\\end{aligned}\n$$",
