      "math_academy_id": "q-11359",
      "knowledge_point_id": "3c22b8e9-049a-5574-86c9-35788c410421",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Binomial Quadratic Factor",
      "problem": "Evaluate $\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x+42}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "The quadratic factor ${x}^{2}+9$ is irreducible, so we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+42}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-3)}=\\frac{Ax+B}{{x}^{2}+9}+\\frac{C}{x-3}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $({x}^{2}+9)(x-3),$ and we get\n\n$$\n{x}^{2}+x+42=(Ax+B)(x-3)+C({x}^{2}+9).\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=-2,B=-5,$ and $C=3.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}+x+42}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-3)}=-\\frac{2x+5}{{x}^{2}+9}+\\frac{3}{x-3}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x+42}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{2x+5}{{x}^{2}+9}+\\frac{3}{x-3})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+9}\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+9}\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we use a substitution $u={x}^{2}+9.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2x\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+9| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+9).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the fact that $\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+{a}^{2}}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{a}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{a}),$ which results in\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+9}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3}).\n$$\n\nFinally, for the third integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|.\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{{x}^{2}+x+42}{({x}^{2}+9)(x-3)}\\,\\text{d}x & =-\\int \\frac{2x}{{x}^{2}+9}\\text{d}x-5\\int \\frac{1}{{x}^{2}+9}\\text{d}x+3\\int \\frac{1}{x-3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+9)-5\\cdot \\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+3\\cdot \\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+9)-\\frac{5}{3}\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(\\frac{x}{3})+3\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-3|+K\\end{aligned}\n$$",
