    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-49873",
      "knowledge_point_id": "116c34e0-5cfd-5bb3-964d-9f2713592207",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Trinomial Quadratic Factor",
      "problem": "Calculate $\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+2x+1}{x({x}^{2}+x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a negative discriminant:\n\n$$\nD={1}^{2}-4(1)(1)=-3<0\n$$\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}+2x+1}{x({x}^{2}+x+1)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{Bx+C}{{x}^{2}+x+1}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $x({x}^{2}+x+1),$ and we get\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}+2x+1=A({x}^{2}+x+1)+(Bx+C)x.\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=1,B=2,$ and $C=1.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}+2x+1}{x({x}^{2}+x+1)}=\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x+1}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+2x+1}{x({x}^{2}+x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{x}+\\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x+1})\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x+1}\\,\\text{d}x\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|.\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}+x+1.$ Then $\\text{d}u=(2x+1)\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x+1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+x+1| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+x+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+2x+1}{x({x}^{2}+x+1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{2x+1}{{x}^{2}+x+1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{2}+x+1)+K\\end{aligned}\n$$",
