    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-3617",
      "knowledge_point_id": "116c34e0-5cfd-5bb3-964d-9f2713592207",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Trinomial Quadratic Factor",
      "problem": "$\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+9x-4}{(x-1)({x}^{2}+4x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x=$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a discriminant that is not a perfect square:\n\n$$\nD={4}^{2}-4(1)(-1)=20\n$$\n\nWe have that $\\sqrt{20}$ is not a rational number, which implies that the quadratic factor doesn't factor over the rational numbers.\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}+9x-4}{(x-1)({x}^{2}+4x-1)}=\\frac{A}{x-1}+\\frac{Bx+C}{{x}^{2}+4x-1}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $(x-1)({x}^{2}+4x-1),$ and we get\n\n$$\n3{x}^{2}+9x-4=A({x}^{2}+4x-1)+(Bx+C)(x-1)\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=2,B=1$ and $C=2.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3{x}^{2}+9x-4}{(x-1)({x}^{2}+4x-1)}=\\frac{2}{x-1}+\\frac{x+2}{{x}^{2}+4x-1}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+9x-4}{(x-1)({x}^{2}+4x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{2}{x-1}+\\frac{x+2}{{x}^{2}+4x-1})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{x+2}{{x}^{2}+4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n2\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x=2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|.\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $u={x}^{2}+4x-1.$ Then $\\text{d}u=2(x+2)\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{x+2}{{x}^{2}+4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\frac{\\text{d}u}{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-1|.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{3{x}^{2}+9x-4}{(x-1)({x}^{2}+4x-1)}\\,\\text{d}x & =2\\int \\frac{1}{x-1}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{x+2}{{x}^{2}+4x-1}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x-1|+\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡|{x}^{2}+4x-1|+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
