    {
      "math_academy_id": "q-115712",
      "knowledge_point_id": "116c34e0-5cfd-5bb3-964d-9f2713592207",
      "knowledge_point": "Integrating a Rational Function With an Irreducible Trinomial Quadratic Factor",
      "problem": "Evaluate the integral  $\\int \\frac{12-5x}{x(2{x}^{2}+5x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x.$",
      "worked_solution": "Notice that the quadratic factor in the denominator has a discriminant that is not a perfect square:\n\n$$\nD=(5)^{2}-4(2)(-6)=73\n$$\n\nWe have that $\\sqrt{73}$ is not a rational number, which implies that the quadratic factor doesn't factor over the rational numbers.\n\nSo, we proceed with the following partial fraction decomposition:\n\n$$\n\\frac{12-5x}{x(2{x}^{2}+5x-6)}=\\frac{A}{x}+\\frac{Bx+C}{2{x}^{2}+5x-6}\n$$\n\nTo determine the coefficients $A,B,$ and $C,$ we first multiply both sides of the above equation by $x(2{x}^{2}+5x-6),$ and we get\n\n$$\n12-5x=A(2{x}^{2}+5x-6)+(Bx+C)x\n$$\n\nSolving for the unknown constants using the usual methods, we get $A=-2,B=4$, and $C=5.$ Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{12-5x}{x(2{x}^{2}+5x-6)}=-\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{4x+5}{2{x}^{2}+5x-6}.\n$$\n\nWe now integrate this function term by term, adding the constant of integration at the very end.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{12-5x}{x(2{x}^{2}+5x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (-\\frac{2}{x}+\\frac{4x+5}{2{x}^{2}+5x-6})\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{4x+5}{2{x}^{2}+5x-6}\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFor the first integral, we have\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|.\n$$\n\nFor the second integral, we use the substitution $u=2{x}^{2}+5x-6.$ Then $\\text{d}u=(4x+5)\\,\\text{d}x,$ and we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{4x+5}{2{x}^{2}+5x-6}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int (\\frac{1}{u})\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|u| \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2{x}^{2}+5x-6|\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get the following result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{12-5x}{x(2{x}^{2}+5x-6)}\\,\\text{d}x & =-2\\int \\frac{1}{x}\\,\\text{d}x+\\int \\frac{4x+5}{2{x}^{2}+5x-6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡|x|+\\operatorname{ln}⁡|2{x}^{2}+5x-6|+K.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "answer_fields": [
